00:00:12.511 --> 00:00:14.781
ZENDAYA:
<i>I got on the phone with Sam
after I watched the pilot.</i>

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.684 line:0%
He was like, "Yeah,
I want to do a musical number,

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:19.718 line:0%
and it'll be beautiful,
and it'll be heartbreaking."

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:23.555 line:0%
I was, you know, listening to
this Labrinth track "All for Us"

00:00:23.622 --> 00:00:25.791
<i> and there was something
 that was so big</i>

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:28.094
<i>and triumphant and beautiful.</i>

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:30.763
LABRINTH:<i> Sam got that energy
 from it, and was like,</i>

00:00:30.829 --> 00:00:32.264
<i>this really feels like Rue.</i>

00:00:32.465 --> 00:00:34.401 line:0%
And when he told me he wanted
to use it for a musical,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:37.136 line:0%
I was like, "Okay!"
I was like, "Bro, that's crazy."

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:39.806
♪<i> Doing it all for love</i> ♪

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.341
ZENDAYA:<i> Lab's a visionary,
 and when he told me</i>

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:44.143
<i> that I would be able
 to record it,</i>

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.945
I was like, "Are you joking?!"

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.213
She listened to my version...

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:50.449
♪<i> Taking it all for us
 All</i> ♪

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.218
LABRINTH:<i> She was like,
 I'm not gonna do that,</i>

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:53.719
<i>but I'm gonna do my version.</i>

00:00:53.819 --> 00:00:56.456
♪<i> Taking it all for us all</i> ♪

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:59.158
That's the perfect way
of approaching the music.

00:00:59.224 --> 00:01:00.726
♪<i> Oh, oh, oh, oh</i> ♪

00:01:00.926 --> 00:01:04.530
LABRINTH:
<i>Sam came up with the idea
 to add a marching band,</i>

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.933
<i>and an even bigger choir,
'cause we wanted to make sure</i>

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:08.368
it was very massive.

00:01:08.435 --> 00:01:10.837 line:0%
Percussion came in,
and they did their parts.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:13.706
(DRUMS BEATING)

00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:20.814
And then we had
the woodwinds and the brass.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.450
(WIND INSTRUMENTS PLAYING)

00:01:32.558 --> 00:01:33.993
DON ROBERTS:
<i> I'm watching Zendaya,</i>

00:01:34.059 --> 00:01:35.461
<i> and I was watching her
 watch the band,</i>

00:01:35.527 --> 00:01:36.662
<i> and I could only
 look at her reactions,</i>

