and I said, "Wow, she must
like that. It's pretty cool."

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.133
JEN MALONE:
<i>The choir totally got into it.</i>

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.868
<i> They were connecting
 with the song,</i>

00:01:42.935 --> 00:01:43.836
and they were having fun.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.639
<i> It just got bigger
 and bigger and bigger.</i>

00:01:48.942 --> 00:01:51.177
SAM LEVINSON:<i> Ryan Heffington
 was our choreographer.</i>

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:53.513 line:0%
My job was to wrangle
200 people.

00:01:53.746 --> 00:01:55.515
<i> It's not always
 just choreographing,</i>

00:01:55.582 --> 00:01:59.485
but it's also infusing
the scene with an importance.

00:01:59.619 --> 00:02:01.954
LEVINSON:<i> When I saw it
 out in the streets,</i>

